SUMMARY

  Implemented ROADMAP.md Milestone 5 for Tamlinux 0.7.0 Northern Torch:
  - Extended `src/desktop/shell/host/protocol_model.js` and
    `ProtocolState.qml` with opt-in `perOutput` and `allowMultipleActive`
    modes (default false, preserving Hyprland and ProtocolShadow
    behaviour), per-output `activeWorkspaceIds`, and output-targeted
    `activate(number, outputName)` / `deactivate(number, outputName)`.
    Guarded `ProtocolState.currentSets()` under `QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen`.
  - Added pure parser/model `src/desktop/shell/host/tam_pane_model.js`
    and native Unix-socket adapter `src/desktop/shell/host/TamPaneAdapter.qml`
    using `ProtocolState` for standard Wayland facts and `Quickshell.Io.Socket`
    connections to `$TAM_PANE_SOCKET` for IPC queries, event streaming,
    actions, multi-tag visibility, windows spanning multiple tags,
    `KeybindingsModel`-compatible JSON binds, keyboard layout tracking,
    on-demand pointer queries, and automatic reconnection with bounded
    backoff.
  - Extended `src/desktop/shell/host/Compositor.qml` to select
    `TamPaneAdapter.qml` when `TAMLINUX_COMPOSITOR_BACKEND=tam-pane`,
    `TAM_PANE_SOCKET` is set, or `XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP` contains
    `tam-pane` (defaulting to `HyprlandAdapter.qml`), and forwarded
    optional output targeting plus `toggleWorkspace(id, outputName)`.
  - Pinned `tam-pane` 0.2.7 (`418bd62de05a3af119064523f81d277913e0711f`)
    in `components.lock`.
  - Added per-output multi-active protocol fixture tests in
    `tests/fixtures/protocol/shell.qml` and the two-output mock (with
    forced disconnect/reconnect) and real headless `tam-pane` test suite
    in `tests/test_tam_pane_adapter.py` and
    `tests/fixtures/tam-pane-adapter/shell.qml`.

